>> title: Chicken and Dumplings
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, dumplings, southern, one-pot, braise, dinner
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: chicken n dumplings, chicken and dropped dumplings, chicken and pastry, stewed chicken and dumplings
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — do not lift the lid to look, because a dumpling cooks in the steam above the broth as much as in it and every peek costs the batch its rise, which does not return; fifteen minutes, then break one open
>> step.1: The whole dish happens in one pot and the dough is the last thing that goes in it. Drop dumplings are stirred in a bowl and spooned onto the surface; rolled ones are cut in strips and dropped in the same way. This is the dropped kind — softer, faster and the one a Tuesday gets.
>> step.2: brown 8 min, skin side down
>> step.3: sweat 6 min
>> step.4: simmer 35 min, pull the meat in
>> step.5: stir a shaggy dough
>> step.6: steam covered 15 min, lid shut
>> step.7: Do not lift the lid to look. A dumpling cooks in the steam above the broth as much as in it, and every peek costs the batch its rise. Fifteen minutes, then the first one broken open to see the middle.

The whole dish happens in one pot and the dough is the last thing that goes in it. Drop dumplings are stirred in a bowl and spooned onto the surface; rolled ones are cut in strips and dropped in the same way. This is the dropped kind — softer, faster and the one a Tuesday gets.

Brown @bone-in chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; skin on) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{8%min}, skin side down.

Sweat @&(~1)browned chicken{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @carrots{3%medium}(sliced in coins), @celery{3%ribs}(sliced) for ~saute{6%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @chicken stock{8%cups}(1.9 L), @bay leaf{1}, @thyme{4%sprigs}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} for ~simmer{35%min}, then lift the chicken out, pull the meat off the bones and return it to the broth.

Stir @all-purpose flour{2%cups}(250 g), @baking powder{1%Tbs}, @cold unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g; grated), @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL) to a shaggy dough that just holds together.

Steam @&(~1)dumpling dough{} in spoonfuls on top of @&(~2)broth{} with @black pepper{1/2%tsp} covered for ~steam{15%min}.

Do not lift the lid to look. A dumpling cooks in the steam above the broth as much as in it, and every peek costs the batch its rise. Fifteen minutes, then the first one broken open to see the middle.
